1
00:00:02,501 --> 00:00:06,882
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let's talk about hindrances in relation to the wild animal.

2
00:00:10,142 --> 00:00:12,263
[SPEAKER_01]: We talked about the fetters last time.

3
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:25,785
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what do hindrances do?

4
00:00:27,225 --> 00:00:31,726
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course, they hinder, but, I mean, more specifically, or differently described,

5
00:00:36,187 --> 00:00:41,572
[SPEAKER_01]: Why are they particularly... well, why do they pertain to the wild animal, not to you?

6
00:00:46,016 --> 00:01:00,149
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, it's also described as corruptions of mind, weaknesses of wisdom.

7
00:01:00,189 --> 00:01:00,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

8
00:01:00,609 --> 00:01:01,170
[SPEAKER_02]: What does it do?

9
00:01:03,453 --> 00:01:05,673
[SPEAKER_02]: What does the hindrance do to the animal, the wild animal?

10
00:01:05,853 --> 00:01:07,174
[SPEAKER_01]: What does it do to... That's just wildness.

11
00:01:07,994 --> 00:01:08,234
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no.

12
00:01:08,254 --> 00:01:12,535
[SPEAKER_01]: What does it do to the... to your experience as a whole?

13
00:01:14,715 --> 00:01:24,597
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is it... What does the hindrance do to the relationship of... between you and the wild animal?

14
00:01:26,877 --> 00:01:27,397
[SPEAKER_03]: Obscures it.

15
00:01:27,437 --> 00:01:27,657
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

16
00:01:28,657 --> 00:01:29,118
[SPEAKER_01]: Which part?

17
00:01:30,918 --> 00:01:31,698
[SPEAKER_03]: The relationship.

18
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:33,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Which part of it?

19
00:01:37,574 --> 00:01:43,219
[SPEAKER_03]: I suppose the access, like the capacity to access.

20
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:44,120
[SPEAKER_01]: What?

21
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,080
[SPEAKER_01]: The wild animal.

22
00:01:45,341 --> 00:01:46,582
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it obscures the wild animal.

23
00:01:46,622 --> 00:01:48,683
[SPEAKER_03]: It obscures the space in between.

24
00:01:49,144 --> 00:01:49,364
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

25
00:01:50,104 --> 00:01:55,509
[SPEAKER_03]: And makes it muddy, makes it cloudy, makes it colored.

26
00:01:56,711 --> 00:02:05,501
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, makes it overlooked, underlooked, over-intended, under-intended.

27
00:02:05,981 --> 00:02:15,772
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what would be the first and foremost thing you would do in regard to any hindrance then, to not fall into overlooking the mind, underlooking it, missing it?

28
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:29,452
[SPEAKER_00]: It's killing the precepts, isn't it?

29
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:30,753
[SPEAKER_01]: More, more specifically now.

30
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:35,056
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all taken for granted that you're already doing that, because you wouldn't be seeing the mind otherwise.

31
00:02:36,037 --> 00:02:37,818
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I mean, directly in relation to the hindrances.

32
00:02:39,779 --> 00:02:45,383
[SPEAKER_01]: What can you do when the hindrance is present, the mind is obscured?

33
00:02:45,743 --> 00:02:49,826
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you get it back?

34
00:02:49,886 --> 00:02:51,347
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't act out of the hindrances.

35
00:02:53,195 --> 00:02:59,940
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't act out, that obviously would prevent things from getting worse, but it would still not necessarily remove the hindrance.

36
00:03:00,641 --> 00:03:11,169
[SPEAKER_03]: And at the same time, which is also not immediately removing the hindrance, but you don't try to directly get rid of the hindrance.

37
00:03:11,189 --> 00:03:12,130
[SPEAKER_03]: The hindrance, yeah.

38
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:17,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that would... What is those... what do those two things have in common?

39
00:03:18,115 --> 00:03:22,038
[SPEAKER_01]: So, not acting out of the hindrance and not trying to directly remove the hindrance.

40
00:03:22,905 --> 00:03:23,786
[SPEAKER_01]: What's the common thread?

41
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:30,251
[SPEAKER_01]: For both.

42
00:03:32,893 --> 00:03:34,474
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why would you be acting out of a hindrance?

43
00:03:35,475 --> 00:03:36,636
[SPEAKER_02]: Let's... let's ask like that.

44
00:03:41,063 --> 00:03:42,925
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you don't want to enjoy it.

45
00:03:42,945 --> 00:03:44,966
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, because it's pressuring you and it's painful.

46
00:03:45,527 --> 00:03:47,509
[SPEAKER_01]: Why would you want to be trying to get rid of the hindrance?

47
00:03:47,529 --> 00:03:49,731
[SPEAKER_03]: Because it's not wanting to enjoy the pressure of it.

48
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:49,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

49
00:03:50,211 --> 00:03:53,474
[SPEAKER_01]: So, both types of actions would really be rooted in hindrance.

50
00:03:54,155 --> 00:03:54,335
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

51
00:03:55,796 --> 00:04:01,061
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the first thing you have to do if you want to get back to seeing your mind.

52
00:04:01,942 --> 00:04:07,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Make sure that no act by body, speech or mind is rooted in hindrance.

53
00:04:08,626 --> 00:04:09,827
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you make sure that?

54
00:04:10,088 --> 00:04:11,089
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you make sure that?

55
00:04:11,129 --> 00:04:13,932
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you do that?

56
00:04:16,175 --> 00:04:21,460
[SPEAKER_01]: Because whatever you want to attempt to do, is rooted in hindrance.

57
00:04:22,782 --> 00:04:23,523
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what do you do then?

58
00:04:25,141 --> 00:04:31,583
[SPEAKER_03]: The basic thing is to question the motivation, the intention behind whatever you are doing.

59
00:04:31,603 --> 00:04:32,664
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that will reveal it.

60
00:04:33,204 --> 00:04:34,805
[SPEAKER_01]: But what does that lead to then?

61
00:04:34,865 --> 00:04:38,766
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you then address the actual... because the hindrance is still there in the way, so to speak.

62
00:04:40,227 --> 00:04:41,987
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're still not revealing the mind.

63
00:04:43,828 --> 00:04:45,568
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, as I said, you're not making it worse.

64
00:04:46,189 --> 00:04:47,289
[SPEAKER_01]: You're still not revealing it.

65
00:04:48,469 --> 00:04:48,690
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

66
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,591
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever you attend to,

67
00:04:53,857 --> 00:04:56,238
[SPEAKER_01]: will be coming out of hindrance.

68
00:04:57,738 --> 00:04:58,679
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you bypass that?

69
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:06,982
[SPEAKER_01]: What is a single factor that would remove the hindering aspect of a hindrance?

70
00:05:07,002 --> 00:05:11,343
[SPEAKER_00]: What is a single thing you can actually develop?

71
00:05:14,705 --> 00:05:15,465
[SPEAKER_03]: Correct attention.

72
00:05:19,866 --> 00:05:22,987
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the single reason that you're hindered.

73
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:29,048
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the single reason that everything you attend to is rooted in hindrance.

74
00:05:30,509 --> 00:05:36,930
[SPEAKER_01]: Because without yoniso of your manasikāra, the yoniso of your manasikāra becomes a hindrance.

75
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:38,731
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the hindrance.

76
00:05:39,291 --> 00:05:44,772
[SPEAKER_01]: So, although you're attending this and that and counterpart and stuff, all of... yoniso of that is the hindrance.

77
00:05:44,952 --> 00:05:48,573
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you want to push the yoniso further, where it's not the hindrance.

78
00:05:51,547 --> 00:05:52,188
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is the mind?

79
00:05:53,669 --> 00:06:15,786
[SPEAKER_01]: So, through not acting out of the pressure of the hindrance, you stay on the level where you know the mind is, even if you're not seeing it, and then balancing the womb, the inside of whatever's being attended, pushing for that perspective, but for that context, and the mind's there.

80
00:06:16,286 --> 00:06:17,547
[SPEAKER_01]: That is what the mind will be.

81
00:06:19,539 --> 00:06:31,232
[SPEAKER_01]: So, although then the tendency to the hindrance might be still present, and if you distract yourself from yoniso manasikāra, you become hindered again.

82
00:06:31,592 --> 00:06:34,676
[SPEAKER_01]: But you cannot be hindered for as long as yoniso manasikāra is established.

83
00:06:34,816 --> 00:06:35,316
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

84
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:38,100
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter the amount of the pressure of the hindrance.

85
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:57,070
[SPEAKER_01]: But now that we got it out of the way, yes, not allowing pressuring images to take the center stage would be one way of re-establishing the balance.

86
00:06:58,410 --> 00:07:05,932
[SPEAKER_01]: Not acting out out of the body, speech, or mind, not giving in to the pressure would be another way of re-establishing the balance.

87
00:07:05,972 --> 00:07:15,915
[SPEAKER_01]: But the reason is you have to know that you have to be seeing past the hindrance through it to be unhindered, not to remove it or deal with it.

88
00:07:17,347 --> 00:07:26,171
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you easily, kind of, especially when it gets into these subtler levels, would fall into, kind of, a tendency, that's still there to some degree, to try to address it.

89
00:07:26,991 --> 00:07:29,532
[SPEAKER_01]: As if, like, no, no, no, if I remove this, the mind will be seen.

90
00:07:29,632 --> 00:07:29,772
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

91
00:07:29,812 --> 00:07:36,515
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind is not seen, not because of the hindrance, but because your attention chose to rest on the hindrance, indirectly, as the basis.

92
00:07:37,976 --> 00:07:40,497
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that needs to be bypassed.

93
00:07:41,717 --> 00:07:43,198
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not something you can directly attend to.

94
00:07:45,212 --> 00:07:57,115
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's through that peripheral knowledge of what you're attending, that's what you then have to work on and keep looking further, to contain the hindrance rightly and to not be hindered by it.

95
00:07:58,835 --> 00:08:07,677
[SPEAKER_01]: And then also see, like as I said before, sometimes, if desire to see the mind is too strong, well, that will be the reason you won't be seeing the mind.

96
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:16,963
[SPEAKER_01]: If the intention, if the craving is too determined to see it, that will be the reason for obscuring it.

97
00:08:19,924 --> 00:08:23,046
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why goes hand... yoniso manasikāra goes hand in hand with knowledge.

98
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:35,352
[SPEAKER_01]: See, if you're not overdoing it, what you're left with is... well, you know that the space in between is there, whether you attend to it or not, whether you know it... whether you're aware of it or not, it has to be there.

99
00:08:36,472 --> 00:08:40,054
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that knowledge already... already establishes a degree of balance.

100
00:08:40,752 --> 00:08:46,758
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, of course, within that, you're going to have more subtle pressures coming up, but the principle remains the same.

101
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:59,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Whereas knowledge has to be developed to the point where it becomes unshakable, regardless of what's being forced, what's forcing itself in between, to obscure it.

102
00:09:02,906 --> 00:09:14,208
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why mindfulness is always the basis of like, well, you can be doubting and not seeing the mind and all of this, but fundamentally, you recollect the basic context and then you know, okay, well, it is within this.

103
00:09:14,528 --> 00:09:15,529
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be outside of this.

104
00:09:16,829 --> 00:09:19,189
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, just retrace your steps in that manner.

105
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,810
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't want to be dealing with hindrances yourself.

106
00:09:25,491 --> 00:09:30,992
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to be, basically, setting up

107
00:09:34,597 --> 00:09:35,978
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind to deal with it.

108
00:09:36,999 --> 00:09:37,459
[SPEAKER_01]: The animal.

109
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:44,504
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you set it up by not taking it at face value and acting out and trying to counter it or get rid of it.

110
00:09:45,885 --> 00:09:57,094
[SPEAKER_01]: And then your work is, while the hindrance is pressuring you, to increase the depth of your yoniso, let's put it that way, so that the mind is discerned in regard to the hindrance.

111
00:09:57,614 --> 00:10:00,216
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like, okay, it's gone, now I can go back to the mind.

112
00:10:00,336 --> 00:10:00,676
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

113
00:10:01,317 --> 00:10:02,598
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind needs to learn.

114
00:10:03,915 --> 00:10:06,716
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the mind's problem, which obviously makes it your problem.

115
00:10:35,975 --> 00:10:42,080
[SPEAKER_01]: So, first, you don't act out of it, so you don't fall into a trap.

116
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:56,032
[SPEAKER_01]: Second, you recollect, you remember, you revisit the fact that the mind has to be there, even if it's not seen, and that it should not be seen at the expense of removing a hindrance.

117
00:10:56,072 --> 00:11:01,056
[SPEAKER_01]: It should be seen through the hindrance, so that both are there, so to speak.

118
00:11:02,249 --> 00:11:07,093
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how the mind gets to know about hindrances and the problem of them.

119
00:11:07,433 --> 00:11:14,579
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, exactly, there won't be hindrances anymore.

120
00:11:17,742 --> 00:11:17,962
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

121
00:11:18,543 --> 00:11:23,247
[SPEAKER_01]: Checking on your intentions, it's another way of regaining, re-establishing the balance.

122
00:11:24,848 --> 00:11:28,351
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, what... why am I...

123
00:11:30,430 --> 00:11:33,591
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to to re-establish the balance of the mind now.

124
00:11:34,052 --> 00:11:35,632
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it because I'm not seeing it, really?

125
00:11:36,413 --> 00:11:39,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Or because I was pressured by something and I'm just needing to deal with it?

126
00:11:41,215 --> 00:11:43,896
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's like, oh, well, that's why I won't be balancing it rightly.

127
00:11:44,776 --> 00:11:46,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Because I'm acting out of such such an intention.

128
00:11:48,956 --> 00:11:58,282
[SPEAKER_01]: So, being able to see yourself doing things... Yeah, that's always... that step is the first one and it never disappears, it never ceases.

129
00:11:58,462 --> 00:12:00,963
[SPEAKER_01]: You always have to be able to see yourself doing or not doing.

130
00:12:02,144 --> 00:12:02,984
[SPEAKER_03]: While you're doing it.

131
00:12:03,024 --> 00:12:03,685
[SPEAKER_01]: While you're doing it.

132
00:12:03,865 --> 00:12:04,065
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

133
00:12:04,205 --> 00:12:04,765
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the point.

134
00:12:04,785 --> 00:12:05,646
[SPEAKER_03]: Before or after.

135
00:12:05,666 --> 00:12:05,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

136
00:12:09,402 --> 00:12:25,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's said, it's said in the dosuttas, we mentioned it before as well, in the talks, like when agreeable perceptions come up, wrongly, not attending them with yoniso, they are hindrance.

137
00:12:27,813 --> 00:12:32,196
[SPEAKER_01]: When disagreeable perceptions come up, absence of yoniso, they are a hindrance.

138
00:12:33,256 --> 00:12:36,518
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if they're attended with yoniso, those things remain.

139
00:12:37,559 --> 00:12:39,040
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the hindering aspect that's gone.

140
00:12:44,643 --> 00:12:49,086
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to bring up the animal and clarify it while being pressured.

141
00:12:49,947 --> 00:12:51,248
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you deal with it rightly.

142
00:12:51,548 --> 00:13:01,575
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how the animal learns to calm down in regard to it and not be agitated by the presence of hindrances towards these certain directions of action and so on.

143
00:13:05,678 --> 00:13:10,422
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you can clearly see, ah, the possibility of that hindrance is between the two of us.

144
00:13:12,027 --> 00:13:20,393
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, the animal is hindered and I don't see it on account of it if I keep... well, you won't be seeing it because you end up acting out of it and not paying attention to your actions anymore.

145
00:13:21,213 --> 00:13:27,217
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you don't act out of it, it doesn't matter how obscure the animal is, you can always recollect the knowledge that it has to be there.

146
00:13:29,239 --> 00:13:36,924
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you can then, on top of that, recollect the knowledge that you shouldn't be trying to get rid of the hindrance that brings it even closer to the animal.

147
00:13:37,104 --> 00:13:38,765
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you can recollect the knowledge that

148
00:13:41,805 --> 00:13:47,009
[SPEAKER_01]: Attending through the hindrance brings up the animal while the hindrance is there.

149
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:49,690
[SPEAKER_01]: Because is the hindrance felt?

150
00:13:50,651 --> 00:13:50,871
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

151
00:13:51,352 --> 00:13:53,333
[SPEAKER_01]: There you go.

152
00:13:53,593 --> 00:13:54,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Who's feeling the hindrance?

153
00:13:55,875 --> 00:13:56,575
[SPEAKER_01]: You or the animal?

154
00:13:56,615 --> 00:13:56,995
[SPEAKER_00]: The animal.

155
00:13:57,296 --> 00:13:57,736
[SPEAKER_01]: There you go.

156
00:13:58,456 --> 00:14:02,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Clarify the feeling of the hindrance, you got back the image of the animal.

157
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:06,242
[SPEAKER_00]: So the only thing you have to get rid of is the action?

158
00:14:07,683 --> 00:14:10,405
[SPEAKER_01]: On your part, yes, and the ignorance on the animal's part.

159
00:14:12,349 --> 00:14:19,134
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's, I mean, like, it's the... it's about what you do, but then also you gotta now teach the animal the right course of action as well.

160
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:26,280
[SPEAKER_01]: To not resist it, to not... not try to get rid of it, to not, as I said, be agitated by the presence of it.

161
00:14:27,481 --> 00:14:29,863
[SPEAKER_01]: They would then push you... try to push you towards action.

162
00:14:32,665 --> 00:14:33,766
[SPEAKER_01]: But, yes, so animal feels.

163
00:14:37,658 --> 00:14:38,398
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't doubt that.

164
00:14:38,538 --> 00:14:39,379
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't doubt the feeling.

165
00:14:39,499 --> 00:14:40,979
[SPEAKER_01]: You can doubt whether the animal feels or not.

166
00:14:41,039 --> 00:14:51,802
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you would have not acted out of the pressing hindrance, if you would have maintained the context of yoniso and nisigāra, you would have recollected what's being felt there.

167
00:14:52,043 --> 00:14:57,824
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the animal feeling the hindrance that you are now correctly attending all of it.

168
00:14:59,585 --> 00:15:02,686
[SPEAKER_01]: So, simply by feeling the hindrance, the animal is revealed.

169
00:15:04,266 --> 00:15:04,867
[SPEAKER_01]: And true feeling.

170
00:15:04,887 --> 00:15:05,747
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't stop feeling it.

171
00:15:07,035 --> 00:15:17,457
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, okay, so it's the animal that needs to deactivate itself, calm down, basically, to the extent that it has been agitated by the hindrance.

172
00:15:17,877 --> 00:15:18,797
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's my task.

173
00:15:19,017 --> 00:15:20,137
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not to remove the hindrance.

174
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:28,979
[SPEAKER_01]: It's to calm the animal while the hindrance is there, repeatedly, until it basically stops being agitated by it.

175
00:15:31,299 --> 00:15:36,060
[SPEAKER_01]: And when the animal is not agitated by the five hindrances, what happens then?

176
00:15:39,671 --> 00:15:40,592
[SPEAKER_01]: What did the sutra say?

177
00:15:44,154 --> 00:15:44,594
[SPEAKER_02]: Jhāna.

178
00:15:45,315 --> 00:15:45,615
[SPEAKER_02]: Jhāna.

179
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:48,897
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes.

180
00:15:49,477 --> 00:15:50,598
[SPEAKER_02]: Your mind is luminous.

181
00:15:52,079 --> 00:15:53,420
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's safe.

182
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:56,182
[SPEAKER_01]: It's secluded from unwholesome states.

183
00:15:57,503 --> 00:16:08,290
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the animal... you seclude the animal not by hiding it in a dungeon, but by teaching it to remain immovable towards the fire.

184
00:16:10,403 --> 00:16:27,994
